Keep discrimination-net cost estimation bounded for large generic functions.

Lem's EXECUTE has over 1,100 methods. SBCL 2.5.10 spends roughly 70 ms per
estimate, twice on early keystrokes, before selecting cached dispatch anyway.
The existing cost limit bounds estimated dispatch cost, not analysis work.
For more than 256 methods, choose SBCL's ordinary cached dispatch directly.
This changes a strategy heuristic, not method applicability or combination;
method/class changes and EQL specializers keep their existing cache handling.

--- a/src/pcl/dfun.lisp
+++ b/src/pcl/dfun.lisp
@@ -609,6 +609,12 @@
   (when (eq **boot-state** 'complete)
     (unless (or caching-p
                 (gf-requires-emf-keyword-checks gf)
+                ;; Avoid lengthy analysis on a cold call or after a method
+                ;; change. The cost estimator's LIMIT does not bound how
+                ;; much work it does before finding a discriminating test.
+                ;; NTHCDR bounds this guard's own traversal as well.
+                (nthcdr 256 (generic-function-methods gf))
+
                 ;; DISPATCH-DFUN-COST will error if it encounters a
                 ;; method with a non-standard specializer.
                 (gf-has-method-with-nonstandard-specializer-p gf))
